    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234-a8">

                <pb facs="0358" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg270"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Captain Miller.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo
                                City, D. R.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to express to you, as the
                    captain of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi>, the thanks of my
                    legation for the response to my request for an armed guard to bring the German
                    vice-consul, Mr. Thorman, and family from his residence to the city.</p>
                <p>I also desire in this connection to commend to you the excellent judgment of
                    Lieutenant Long, in charge of the marine corps, and the perfect discipline of
                    the men in his command.</p>
                <p>I shall with pleasure make this statement in my dispatches to the Secretary of
                    State of your ready response and the perfect discipline of your command.</p>
                <p>It also affords me further pleasure to say that I am glad that this aid was
                    rendered to one in the consular service of His Imperial Majesty the German
                    Emperor.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
